{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789742290,"nonce":"oq+y4V5J3rshBQMSAJNqjrrzWmA=","message":"Inheritance and overloads landed in e3a66ef:\n\n- The macro emits `Panel extends Hud` when the Wren superclass is a\n  class of the same module (else `caribou.Ref`, as before: a Haxe or\n  another module's superclass has no emitted class). The subclass\n  declares its own instance members only; an override is reached\n  through the superclass's wrapper, since the native sends to the\n  object and Wren dispatches. Statics of the chain are declared on the\n  subclass (Haxe does not inherit statics, Wren does) and sent to the\n  subclass's class object, resolved through the registry's superclass\n  chain (import.rs static_in_chain).\n- Constructors: the subclass's `new` calls `super()` with placeholders\n  (0, false, null by type), and the superclass's constructor native\n  binds nothing to an instance of a subclass that has a constructor of\n  its own; a subclass without one inherits it, as in Wren, and the\n  native constructs the subclass through it. Both tell the case by the\n  fresh object's own hl_type (import.rs constructs).\n- Overloads keep the arity suffix (`draw1`), now also against names an\n  emitted superclass takes; documented in haxe-imports.md.\n- Found on the way: CallSite::clear_direct left `a`/`b` holding the\n  direct send's closure and class, which the plain path then read back\n  as the (signature, statics) symbols — \"Panel does not implement\n  'label(_)'\" on the first subclass receiver at a superclass's site.\n  Cleared with the key now (protocol.rs).\n- Test: UseHud.family in haxe_imports.rs (Panel/Badge in hud.wren).\n\nLeft here, the dynamic face. The principled shape is not a reflective\nAPI on caribou.Ref but Haxe's own `Dynamic` access reaching the\nprotocol: ash's hlp_dyn_get/set/call on an object whose type is not\nash's own (a cell: a TypeDesc at word zero) would ask a seam slot\n(`dyn_get(obj, field hash)`, `dyn_set`, `dyn_call(obj, hash, args)`),\nand caribou-ash would answer through the protocol by the field's name\n(ash keeps hash -\u003e name for reflection). Also what makes `d.add(3)` work\nfor a declared class through Dynamic, whose wrappers are inline and so\nnot protos. Needs an ash seam slot; ash's tree is mid-migration to\nedition 2024 (8635a76 does not build), so it waits for that.","files":null}]}